<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{ Title }}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="{{ Description }}">
    {#
      Two theme colours, so a browser's own chrome follows the reader's
      setting instead of picking one and being wrong half the time.
    #}
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#c04058" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#171013" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Tinku">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ SocialDescription }}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
    <link rel="icon" href="assets/tinku-mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

    <header class="site-header" data-header>
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Tinku home">
        <img class="brand__mark" src="assets/tinku-mark.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32">
        <span>Tinku</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="#own">Own it</a>
        <a href="#how">How it works</a>
        <a href="#directories">Directories</a>
        <a class="nav-cta" href="#join">Join in <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="hero__content">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> {{ HeroEyebrow }}</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">
            {{ HeroTitleLead }}<br>
            <em>{{ HeroTitleEmphasis }}</em>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero__lede">{{ HeroLead }}</p>
          <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="button button--primary" href="#join">
              Join the community
              <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            </a>
            <a
              class="button button--secondary"
              href="https://github.com/catalystcommunity/tinku"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              Read the code
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        {#
          A worked example rather than a screenshot: it says what the product
          does in the product's own vocabulary, and it cannot go out of date
          with the UI.
        #}
        <div class="calendar-card" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="calendar-card__heading">
            <span>Thursday Bouldering</span>
            <small>climbers@saltflats.example</small>
          </div>
          <div class="calendar-row">
            <span>10 Sep</span>
            <p><small>19:00 America/Denver</small>Second Thursday Session</p>
          </div>
          <div class="calendar-row">
            <span>08 Oct</span>
            <p><small>19:00 America/Denver</small>Second Thursday Session</p>
          </div>
          <div class="calendar-row calendar-row--remote">
            <span>12 Oct</span>
            <p><small>from forge.example</small>Autumn Climb Meetup</p>
          </div>
          <p class="calendar-card__stamp">One rule. Every second Thursday.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="manifesto" id="own" aria-labelledby="own-title">
        <div class="section-label">
          <span>01</span>
          <p>Own it</p>
        </div>
        <div class="manifesto__body">
          <h2 id="own-title">
            Your community’s events<br>
            belong to <em>your community.</em>
          </h2>
          <div class="manifesto__copy">
            <p>
              Most events live on somebody else’s platform. They set the rules,
              they own the list, and they can change either one — or close the
              door and take the calendar with them.
            </p>
            <p>
              Tinku is open source and runs anywhere. One community, one
              instance, one group of people who decide how it works. Nothing
              about it needs anyone’s permission to keep going.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="platform" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <div class="platform__intro">
          <div class="section-label section-label--light">
            <span>02</span>
            <p>How it works</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2 id="how-title">Built the way<br><em>groups actually meet.</em></h2>
            <p>
              A gathering is the thing people join. Events hang off it — one
              night, or a rule that keeps making them.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-grid">
          <article class="capability">
            <span class="capability__number">01</span>
            <div class="capability__icon" aria-hidden="true">◷</div>
            <h3>Events that repeat</h3>
            <p>
              “The second Thursday at 19:00” is a rule, not fifty copies. It
              stays 19:00 when the clocks change.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="capability">
            <span class="capability__number">02</span>
            <div class="capability__icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</div>
            <h3>Gatherings and organizations</h3>
            <p>
              People join a gathering. An organization can own one, so it
              outlives whoever started it.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="capability">
            <span class="capability__number">03</span>
            <div class="capability__icon" aria-hidden="true">◈</div>
            <h3>Find it by place and time</h3>
            <p>
              Search by city, by distance, by when it starts — across
              everything the instance knows about.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="capability capability--accent">
            <span class="capability__number">04</span>
            <div class="capability__icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>
            <h3>Yours to change</h3>
            <p>
              Open source, an open API, and a schema you can read. Run it, fork
              it, or build something else on it.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="directories" id="directories" aria-labelledby="directories-title">
        <div class="section-label">
          <span>03</span>
          <p>Cross-domain directories</p>
        </div>
        <div class="directories__body">
          <h2 id="directories-title">
            Small and separate,<br>
            still <em>easy to find.</em>
          </h2>
          <div class="directories__copy">
            <p>
              Running your own calendar usually means nobody finds it. Tinku
              fixes that the way email does: instances hand signed copies of
              their events to directories that have agreed to take them.
            </p>
            <p>
              One search then covers many communities at once. Every result
              shows the domain it came from, so a familiar name from somewhere
              else is never mistaken for yours — and the full details always
              live at the source.
            </p>
            <p>
              Both sides opt in. Nothing leaves your instance until you say so,
              and no directory fills up with events it did not agree to carry.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="invitation" id="join" aria-labelledby="join-title">
        <div class="invitation__graphic" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="emblem">
            <span class="emblem__rivet emblem__rivet--one"></span>
            <span class="emblem__rivet emblem__rivet--two"></span>
            <span class="emblem__rivet emblem__rivet--three"></span>
            <span class="emblem__rivet emblem__rivet--four"></span>
            <p>Tinku</p>
            <img class="core-mark" src="assets/tinku-mark.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
            <small>Come and meet</small>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="invitation__content">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Everyone is welcome</p>
          <h2 id="join-title">Bring your<br>community.</h2>
          <p>
            Tinku is early and built in the open. If you run a community, help
            us find out what it still needs. If you write code, there is plenty
            to do.
          </p>
          <div class="invitation__links">
            <a
              class="button button--dark"
              href="https://forgeutah.tech"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              Forge Utah on Slack
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a
              class="button button--ghost"
              href="https://discord.gg/sfNb9xRjPn"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              Catalyst Community Discord
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
            <a
              class="button button--ghost"
              href="https://github.com/catalystcommunity/tinku"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >
              GitHub
              <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <a class="brand brand--footer" href="#top">
        <img class="brand__mark" src="assets/tinku-mark.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32">
        <span>Tinku</span>
      </a>
      <p>Open source community events. &copy; <span data-year>2026</span></p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="https://forgeutah.tech" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Slack ↗</a>
        <a href="https://discord.gg/sfNb9xRjPn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Discord ↗</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/catalystcommunity/tinku" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script src="site.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
